          "what": "NGINX is a high-performance web server, reverse proxy, and load balancer designed to handle massive concurrent connections with minimal resource usage. Its event-driven, asynchronous architecture avoids thread-per-connection overhead, making it ideal for high-traffic sites. Use it to serve static content, terminate SSL, cache responses, or distribute traffic across backend servers. Extend functionality via modules for caching, security, or HTTP/3 support.",
