      "summaries": {
        "en": "MXC is a Rust-based sandbox framework that enforces policy-driven, layered isolation for untrusted code execution. Unlike traditional sandboxes that rely on single mechanisms, MXC combines multiple containment layers (e.g., seccomp, Landlock, Linux namespaces) into a configurable policy. This design allows fine-grained control over system calls, file access, and network, making it ideal for CI/CD pipelines, plugin systems, or running AI-generated code safely. Developers can define custom policies via a simple YAML file, balancing security and functionality without modifying the host system.",
        "zh": "MXC 是一个基于 Rust 的沙箱框架，通过策略驱动的分层隔离机制安全执行不受信任代码。它组合 seccomp、Landlock、Linux 命名空间等多种内核安全机制，形成可配置策略层，实现系统调用、文件访问和网络通信的细粒度控制。开发者无需修改主机系统即可定制安全边界，适用于 CI/CD 流水线、插件系统或 AI 生成代码等高危场景。用户通过简洁 YAML 策略文件灵活权衡安全与功能，Rust 实现确保高性能与内存安全。",
        "es": "MXC is a Rust-based sandbox framework that enforces policy-driven, layered isolation for untrusted code execution. Unlike traditional sandboxes that rely on single mechanisms, MXC combines multiple containment layers (e.g., seccomp, Landlock, Linux namespaces) into a configurable policy. This design allows fine-grained control over system calls, file access, and network, making it ideal for CI/CD pipelines, plugin systems, or running AI-generated code safely. Developers can define custom policies via a simple YAML file, balancing security and functionality without modifying the host system.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "mxc gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "MXC is a Rust-based sandbox framework that enforces policy-driven, layered isolation for untrusted code execution. Unlike traditional sandboxes that rely on single mechanisms, MXC combines multiple containment layers (e.g., seccomp, Landlock, Linux namespaces) into a configurable policy. This design allows fine-grained control over system calls, file access, and network, making it ideal for CI/CD pipelines, plugin systems, or running AI-generated code safely. Developers can define custom policies via a simple YAML file, balancing security and functionality without modifying the host system.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/microsoft/mxc for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
