      "summaries": {
        "en": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 is a compressed version of Qwen's 35B MoE model, using NVFP4 quantization to reduce memory and accelerate inference while retaining most capabilities. The key insight is that 4-bit floating-point quantization (NVFP4) preserves model quality better than integer quantization for MoE architectures. You can deploy it with vLLM for efficient serving, or fine-tune it for domain-specific tasks, making large MoE models practical on limited hardware.",
        "zh": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 是 Qwen 3.6 系列中 35B 参数 MoE 模型的压缩版本，通过 NVFP4 量化技术大幅降低显存占用并加速推理，同时保留大部分原始能力。其技术亮点在于：针对 MoE 架构，采用 4 位浮点量化（NVFP4）相比整数量化能更好保持模型质量，避免专家路由的精度损失。你可以直接使用 vLLM 部署该模型，实现高效服务；或基于它进行领域微调，在资源受限的环境下运行强大的 MoE 模型。适合需要平衡性能与成本的场景，如企业级对话系统或实时推理应用。",
        "es": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 is a compressed version of Qwen's 35B MoE model, using NVFP4 quantization to reduce memory and accelerate inference while retaining most capabilities. The key insight is that 4-bit floating-point quantization (NVFP4) preserves model quality better than integer quantization for MoE architectures. You can deploy it with vLLM for efficient serving, or fine-tune it for domain-specific tasks, making large MoE models practical on limited hardware.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 stands out for safetensors, qwen3_5_moe, and qwen in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 is a compressed version of Qwen's 35B MoE model, using NVFP4 quantization to reduce memory and accelerate inference while retaining most capabilities. The key insight is that 4-bit floating-point quantization (NVFP4) preserves model quality better than integer quantization for MoE architectures. You can deploy it with vLLM for efficient serving, or fine-tune it for domain-specific tasks, making large MoE models practical on limited hardware.",
          "how": "Review https://huggingface.co/RedHatAI/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
